    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d917">

                <pb facs="0718" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13258.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Special Agent Carothers.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please say to General Villa that the President has received his telegram of
                    September 17 in which he expresses his appreciation of the President’s action in
                    ordering the American forces to withdraw from Vera Cruz; that it has given the
                    President much pleasure to receive General Villa’s message; and that he hopes
                    that the withdrawal <pb facs="0719" n="603" xml:id="pg603"/> will be regarded by
                    the Mexican people as another evidence of this Government’s desire to lend its
                    aid to bring about the speedy establishment of a truly just and representative
                    government in Mexico.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
